WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone, and welcome to your second drink of gossip.
大家好，欢迎收听第二杯八卦。

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.600
Well, as you know, this episode starts with the parkour cold open,
如你们所知，这集开场是跑酷的开场白，

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.980
and we got this letter from Ethan C.
我们收到了来自科罗拉多州利特尔顿的伊森·C的信。

4
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.260
in Littleton, Colorado.
伊森说，

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.300
Ethan said,
珍娜和安吉拉，首先，我非常爱你们俩。

6
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.860
Jenna and Angela, first, I love y'all both so much.
谢谢你，伊森。

7
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:19.720
Thanks, Ethan.
《办公室》是我生活中非常重要的一部分，每个人都知道这一点。

8
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.080
The office is such a huge part of my life, and everyone knows it.
我必须分享一件在工作时发生在我身上的事，

9
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.600
I have to share something that happened to me at work,
这也是《办公室》唯一让我失望的一次。

10
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.360
and it's the only time the office has let me down.
不过，我不是在办公室工作。

11
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.120
Now, I don't work in an office.
我在诺克斯维尔的一所宝藏小学工作。

12
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.320
I work in an amazing elementary school in Knoxville.
上周五，我们举办了年度才艺秀。

13
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.500
Well, last Friday, we had our annual talent show.
首先我要说明，我们的才艺秀可不一般。

14
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.820
Now, let me preface by saying we don't have normal talent shows.
我们的才艺秀独一无二。

15
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.560
Ours are like no other.
绝对充满了高光时刻，学生们也都非常优秀。

16
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.620
They're absolutely overflowing with highlights and are wonderful students.
说实话，这太棒了。

17
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:48.960
It's honestly amazing.
精彩的部分来了。

18
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.860
Here's where it gets good.
我们有一群孩子表演了搞笑跑酷，

19
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.780
We had a group of kids do comedic parkour
同时我们在他们身后播放了迈克尔、德怀特和安迪跑酷的视频。

20
00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.380
while we played the video of Michael, Dwight, and Andy parkouring behind them.
我决定也加入进去凑个热闹，为什么不呢？

21
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.920
I decided to join in on the fun because why not?
哦，不。

22
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:05.600
Oh, no.
只能说，我的跑酷劲儿使过头了，

23
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.600
Well, let's just say I parkoured a little too hard,
现在我的前十字韧带撕裂了。

24
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.860
and now I have a torn ACL.
《办公室》让我以为自己会跑酷，其实我根本不会。

25
00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:15.740
The office had me thinking I could parkour, and I park can't.
总之，非常感谢你们，我必须分享这个故事。

26
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.760
Anyways, I appreciate y'all so much and had to share this story.
也许我的信可以作为“第二杯八卦”节目的一则免责声明，

27
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.340
Maybe my letter can be used as a disclaimer on the second drink of gossip
提醒那些不需要跑酷的人。

28
00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.940
for those that need not parkour.
噢，天哪。

29
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.460
Oh, my gosh.
伊森，我们太遗憾了，不过听起来这也像是我会做的事，

30
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.500
Ethan, we're so sorry, but also that sounds like something I would have jumped in
我会直接跳进去说，我要和孩子们一起做。

31
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.260
and been like, I'm going to do it with the kids.
你知道我做了什么吗？

32
00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.580
You know what I did?
你知道克里德说他想做一个完美的侧手翻吗？

33
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:43.600
You know when Creed is talking about how he wants to do one perfect cartwheel?
一个完美的侧手翻，对。

34
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.280
One perfect cartwheel, yeah.
这让我纳闷自己现在还能不能做一个完美的侧手翻。

35
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.640
That made me wonder if I could do a perfect cartwheel anymore.
你最近做过吗？

36
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.040
Did you do one recently?
不是最近。

37
00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.100
Not recently.
大概是10年前，我还四十多岁的时候，结果扭伤了肩膀。

38
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:56.500
This was like even 10 years ago in my 40s, and I threw out my shoulder.
就像我的脖子狠狠地落枕了一样。

39
00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.580
Like, I got a big crick in my neck.
那简直是一场惨剧。

40
00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.680
It was a debacle.
那是一场悲剧。

41
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:01.060
It was a tragedy.
在我的脑海里，我依然能想象出我的身体在空中移动、跳舞的画面，

42
00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:06.120
I still, in my mind, I can imagine my body moving through space, dancing,
因为我从小就跳舞、做侧手翻或者跳水，所有这些。

43
00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:12.420
because I grew up dancing, or cartwheeling, or doing a dive, all these things.
但我已经做不到了。

44
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.140
And I cannot.
我不应该再做了。

45
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.420
I should not.
我想是两年前的夏天，我在前院和孩子们一起做了一个侧手翻。

46
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.920
I did a cartwheel, I think, two summers ago in the front yard with the kids.
结果怎么样？

47
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:21.560
How'd that go?
做完之后我觉得自己就像遭遇了一场车祸。

48
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:25.100
I felt like I was in a car accident afterwards.
是啊。

49
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:25.620
Yeah.
那种感觉就是这样。

50
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.260
That's how it felt.
那种感觉就是这样。

51
00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.200
I was trying to teach my kids how to do a somersault,
我当时在教我的孩子们怎么做前滚翻，

52
00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.840
and it was the worst decision I ever made.
结果这是我做过最糟糕的决定。

53
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:35.680
I was like, this is for the people at the little kiddie gym who are much younger than me.
我心想，这可是给儿童健身房那些比我小得多的人准备的。

54
00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.440
And I used to do cartwheels all over the place, but I did.
我以前到处都能做侧手翻，但我确实做了。

55
00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.220
I sort of like, you know that minor fender bender where you're like,
我有点像，你知道那种轻微的追尾事故，你会觉得，

56
00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.880
oh, my neck is sore and my back.
噢，我的脖子酸痛，还有我的背。

57
00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:43.240
Yeah.
是啊。

58
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.220
And my arm.
还有我的胳膊。

59
00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.220
What's that about?
那是怎么回事？

60
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.060
I mean, it's not like I, I mean, I work out, I lift weights, I stretch.
我的意思是，这倒不是说我，我是说，我锻炼，我举重，我拉伸。

61
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.020
Why can't I do these things?
为什么我做不了这些事情？

62
00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.980
Why can't I move my body like this anymore?
为什么我的身体再也不能这样动了？

63
00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.460
Sam, can you do a cartwheel?
山姆，你会做侧手翻吗？

64
00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.740
You're younger than us.
你比我们年轻。

65
00:02:58.980 --> 00:02:59.780
Absolutely not.
绝对不会。

66
00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:00.680
No.
不会。

67
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.240
No, not in the slighteSt.
不，一点也不会。

68
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.460
I would blow both my shoulders out and my knees.
我的双肩和双膝都会废掉。

69
00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.000
Okay.
好吧。

70
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.060
You know what I did last night I was really proud of?
你知道我昨晚做了什么让我特别自豪的事吗？

71
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.880
I know, Ethan, we're getting off here on a tangent.
我知道，伊桑，我们现在扯远了。

72
00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:14.540
Last night in the pool in the shallow end, I did a perfect handstand and walked across the pool.
昨晚在泳池的浅水区，我做了一个完美的倒立，然后走过了泳池。

73
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.060
See, now water, in water, I think I can do a lot of cool shit.
你看，现在在水里，在水里，我觉得我能做出很多酷炫的事。

74
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.300
Can you do a handstand in the shallow end?
你能在浅水区做倒立吗？

75
00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

76
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.640
Well, report back.
好吧，回头给个反馈。

77
00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.100
All right.
好吧。

78
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.000
Ethan, thank you so much.
伊桑，非常感谢你。

79
00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.600
I hope you're healing and on the mend.
希望你在康复中，身体快点好起来。

80
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.080
We also got a fan mail flurry.
我们还收到了一波粉丝来信。

81
00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.040
Jenna, you might remember that you did a breakdown of the things on Aaron's desk.
珍娜，你可能还记得你盘点过亚伦桌子上的东西。

82
00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:36.380
Yes.
是的。

83
00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:43.400
You thought you spotted a ski boot and a stuffed dog with a little sweater that both said J-R-O-B.
你当时以为自己发现了一只滑雪靴和一个穿着小毛衣的毛绒狗，上面都写着J-R-O-B。

84
00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.320
The only thing you could find that matched that was a wrestling camp, which didn't make any sense.
你能找到与之相符的唯一东西是一个摔跤训练营，这根本说不通。

85
00:03:49.720 --> 00:04:00.960
But a big thank you to Rebecca D, Greg H, Stephanie F, and Dave M, who all wrote in to say that the ski boot and sweater actually say J-F-B-B,
但非常感谢丽贝卡·D、格雷格·H、斯蒂芬妮·F和戴夫·M，他们都写信来说那只滑雪靴和毛衣上其实写的是J-F-B-B，

86
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:05.700
which stands for Jack Frost Big Boulder, a local Scranton ski resort.
代表杰克霜大博尔德，一个当地的斯克兰顿滑雪度假村。

87
00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.500
Well, that makes a lot more sense.
嗯，这样就合理多了。

88
00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.500
It really does.
确实如此。

89
00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.640
Why it's on a ski boot.
难怪它会出现在滑雪靴上。

90
00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.020
Yes.
是的。

91
00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.940
And I guess we've learned that Aaron is a snow skiing enthusiaSt.
我想我们了解到亚伦是个滑雪爱好者。

92
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.480
But also I could see her wrestling.
但我也觉得她会摔跤。

93
00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:27.000
No, I was going to say I could see Aaron just sort of like randomly collecting things from a sport she doesn't play because she's Aaron.
不，我是想说，我能想象亚伦随性地收集一些她根本不玩的运动的周边，因为她就是亚伦。

94
00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:27.620
Yes.
是的。

95
00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.300
I don't know.
我不知道。

96
00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.020
Well, Jonathan A.
好吧，来自洛杉矶的

97
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.560
from Los Angeles wrote in to say,
乔纳森·A写信来说，

98
00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:32.140
Hi there.
嗨，你们好。

99
00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.540
Hoping this gets in when you all take a second drink of gossip.
希望这封信在你们喝第二杯八卦的时候能被念到。

100
00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:43.200
In the scene when Pam and Jim tell the whole team about the pregnancy and everyone is chiming in, Ryan says,
在潘和吉姆向整个团队宣布怀孕消息、大家七嘴八舌的时候，瑞安说，

101
00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:44.520
Don't vaccinate it.
别给她打疫苗。

102
00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.200
Ha ha.
哈哈。

103
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.000
Was that scripted or improv?
那是剧本写的还是即兴发挥？

104
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.240
Love the pod.
超爱这个播客。

105
00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.300
Well, Jonathan, I love this scene.
乔纳森，我很喜欢这场戏。

106
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.500
I love this scene where we're in the conference room.
我很喜欢我们在会议室里的这场戏。

107
00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:02.140
It's at the end of the episode and it becomes clear that Michael has spread all these rumors about people to cover up Stanley's affair.
那是剧集快结束时，大家发现迈克尔为了掩盖斯坦利的婚外情，散布了关于大家的各种谣言。

108
00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:10.400
And just when Michael is about to announce to everyone what the one true thing is, Jim chimes in and he says,
就在迈克尔准备向所有人宣布那个唯一的真事时，吉姆插话了，他说，

109
00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.100
It's us.
是我们。

110
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.160
Pam is pregnant.
帕姆怀孕了。

111
00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.780
And everyone has a little sidebar comment.
每个人都小声嘀咕了一句。

112
00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.720
Actually, I think we should listen to it.
其实，我觉得我们应该听听看。

113
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.200
Okay.
好的。

114
00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.100
You told everyone I was having an affair.
你告诉所有人我有外遇。

115
00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:21.640
Okay.
好吧。

116
00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.140
Okay.
好吧。

117
00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:22.780
Here's the thing.
事情是这样的。

118
00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.340
There was one true rumor out there today.
今天流传的谣言里有一个是真的。

119
00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.660
I didn't want everybody to know what it was.
我本来不想让大家知道是哪个。

120
00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:32.200
So all of you are off the hook except for this one person.
所以你们所有人都没事了，除了这一个人。

121
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.180
Well, then what's the one true rumor?
那真正的谣言到底是什么？

122
00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:35.880
We have a right to know.
我们有权知道。

123
00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.360
Michael, am I gay?
迈克尔，我是同性恋吗？

124
00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:44.580
The one true rumor, and this is going to ruin this person's life, is that...
唯一的真谣言——这会毁了这人的生活——那就是……

125
00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.020
Pam's pregnant.
帕姆怀孕了。

126
00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:46.200
I knew it.
我就知道。

127
00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.360
I knew it.
我就知道。

128
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.060
Her breasts were a tiny bit bigger.
她的胸部稍微变大了一点。

129
00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.800
At first, I thought, oh, she has a new bra with padding.
起初我还想，哦，她换了带胸垫的新胸罩。

130
00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:57.680
But then I thought, Pam doesn't need padding.
但转念一想，帕姆根本不需要胸垫。

131
00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.840
It just didn't add up, Jim.
这根本说不通，吉姆。

132
00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:00.260
Okay.
好吧。

133
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:01.280
Thank you.
谢谢。

134
00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:01.940
Congratulations.
恭喜。

135
00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.600
That's really great, you guys.
真是太棒了，你们俩。

136
00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:04.420
Don't vaccinate it.
别给他打疫苗。

137
00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.100
Who's the father?
孩子是谁的？

138
00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:05.600
Jim.
吉姆的。

139
00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:06.600
How far along?
几个月了？

140
00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:07.440
Four months.
四个月。

141
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:08.980
Who's the OBGYN?
妇产科医生是谁？

142
00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:09.600
Stop, don't.
停下，别说了。

143
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.020
All right.
好吧。

144
00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:10.320
All right.
好吧。

145
00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.040
You know...
你知道的……

146
00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.080
The nosiest group of people.
这是一群最好管闲事的人。

147
00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:17.420
I know.
我知道。

148
00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.340
To answer your question, Jonathan, Ryan's line was scripted.
回答你的问题，乔纳森，瑞恩的台词是剧本写好的。

149
00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.800
All of those sidebar comments were scripted.
所有那些小声嘀咕都是剧本安排的。

150
00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.280
I love how you guys fire them off so quickly.
我太喜欢你们接梗这么快了。

151
00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.420
The scene was so fun to shoot.
这场戏拍得太开心了。

152
00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:36.420
One of my favorite parts is when John as Jim slowly comes over and puts his arm around
我最喜欢的桥段之一，就是约翰饰演的吉姆慢慢走过来，把手搭在

153
00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:42.560
Pam to sort of shield her from Kevin, who's coming up over her shoulder from behind her
帕姆身上，有点像是在保护她免受凯文的干扰，凯文从她身后探过肩膀来

154
00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.320
to talk about her padded bras.
跟她讨论她的加垫胸罩。

155
00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.880
It was very funny.
真的超级搞笑。

156
00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.700
Everyone's at the top of their game in this quick little scene.
