Oh.
哦。

1092
00:48:32.940 --> 00:48:39.800
Michael is still going to march up, but the interns are gossiping as he arrives.
迈克尔还是要大步走过去，但实习生们在他到达时正在八卦。

1093
00:48:39.800 --> 00:48:40.240
Oh.
哦。

1094
00:48:41.360 --> 00:48:41.840
Uh-huh.
呃哼。

1095
00:48:42.280 --> 00:48:47.020
It says, interior break room, Maury, Eric, and Maria, because that's what she was called
上面写着，内景休息室，莫里、埃里克和玛丽亚——因为她在拍摄剧本里叫这个名字——

1096
00:48:47.020 --> 00:48:53.020
in the shooting draft, are in an assembly line style, unstapling and collating and stapling.
正以流水线的方式，在拆订书钉、整理和装订。

1097
00:48:53.500 --> 00:48:54.880
Michael barges in.
迈克尔闯了进去。

1098
00:48:55.460 --> 00:48:58.540
Maury says, you see what Erin's wearing today?
莫里说，你看到艾琳今天穿的什么了吗？

1099
00:48:58.960 --> 00:48:59.460
Eric.
埃里克。

1100
00:48:59.980 --> 00:49:01.800
I'm more of a Pam kind of guy.
我更喜欢潘那款的。

1101
00:49:02.500 --> 00:49:03.100
Maria.
玛丽亚。

1102
00:49:03.540 --> 00:49:07.120
The warehouse guys were saying she's dated like everyone in the office.
仓库的伙计们说她跟办公室里的每个人都约会过。

1103
00:49:07.120 --> 00:49:08.780
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1104
00:49:09.360 --> 00:49:14.080
And then at this moment, Michael says, you stupid son of a bitch.
然后就在这时候，迈克尔说，你这个愚蠢的王八蛋。

1105
00:49:14.080 --> 00:49:15.380
You set me up.
你给我设套。

1106
00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:26.640
Well, this is when it finally occurs to Michael after much explanation that perhaps Stanley was
嗯，在经过一番解释之后，迈克尔终于意识到，也许斯坦利

1107
00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:28.560
there with someone other than his wife.
当时是在跟他的妻子以外的人在一起。

1108
00:49:28.960 --> 00:49:33.020
The amount of time it takes Michael to clue in on something.
迈克尔反应过来一件事所需的时间，

1109
00:49:33.140 --> 00:49:33.780
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1110
00:49:33.900 --> 00:49:35.120
Is one of my favorite things.
是我最喜欢的事情之一。

1111
00:49:35.340 --> 00:49:35.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1112
00:49:35.480 --> 00:49:40.540
Well, now Michael really has some gossip, and he is so excited to share it.
好吧，现在迈克尔真的掌握了一些八卦，他兴奋得急于分享。

1113
00:49:40.660 --> 00:49:45.860
He does not at all understand the gravity of what he's sharing and the damage it could
他完全不明白他所分享的事情的严重性，以及它可能

1114
00:49:45.860 --> 00:49:47.320
do to multiple lives.
对多个家庭造成的破坏。

1115
00:49:47.540 --> 00:49:50.000
He's just giddy to have a little tidbit of info.
他只是为能掌握一点小内幕而欣喜若狂。

1116
00:49:50.200 --> 00:49:54.880
He runs over to the biggest office gossip, Kelly, and he says Stanley's having an affair.
他跑去找办公室最大的八卦王凯莉，说斯坦利有外遇。

1117
00:49:55.240 --> 00:49:56.200
She's like, what?
她一脸惊讶，什么？

1118
00:49:56.440 --> 00:49:59.900
We had a fan catch from Sarah G in Ottawa.
我们收到了来自渥太华的粉丝莎拉·G的发现。

1119
00:50:00.720 --> 00:50:05.480
At around 6 minutes, 30 seconds, when Michael tells Kelly about Stanley's affair, there's
在大约6分30秒时，当迈克尔告诉凯莉关于斯坦利的外遇时，

1120
00:50:05.480 --> 00:50:08.900
a whiteboard behind her desk that reads people's names and numbers.
她办公桌后面有一块白板，上面写着人们的名字和数字。

1121
00:50:09.180 --> 00:50:13.900
It says sales, quarterly sales, and HR performance.
上面写着销售额、季度销售额和人力资源绩效。

1122
00:50:15.500 --> 00:50:22.000
Sarah notes, one, Pam is not on there, even though she is a salesperson now, but Creed is.
莎拉指出，第一，帕姆不在上面，尽管她现在是个销售员了，但克里德在。

1123
00:50:22.260 --> 00:50:24.100
Sarah wants to know why is that?
莎拉想知道这是为什么？

1124
00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:29.460
Sarah, I do not think that this whiteboard has been changed in, like, two seasons.
莎拉，我觉得这块白板大概有两季都没换过了。

1125
00:50:29.740 --> 00:50:30.460
For sure.
肯定的。

1126
00:50:30.680 --> 00:50:33.600
Because I remember seeing this whiteboard in season three.
因为我记得在第三季里见过这块白板。

1127
00:50:34.040 --> 00:50:35.280
Andy is at the top.
安迪在最上面。

1128
00:50:35.760 --> 00:50:39.000
And I don't think I've seen this change in years.
而且我觉得我已经好几年没见它变过了。

1129
00:50:39.360 --> 00:50:42.180
Well, to be fair, we were rarely over in that corner.
嗯，说实话，我们很少去那个角落。

1130
00:50:42.180 --> 00:50:44.760
So, it might have gotten overlooked.
所以，它可能被忽视了。

1131
00:50:45.440 --> 00:50:48.560
Michael is determined to keep spreading this information.
迈克尔决心继续传播这个消息。

1132
00:50:48.720 --> 00:50:51.760
He is now trying to get Kevin to guess.
他现在正试图让凯文猜。

1133
00:50:52.300 --> 00:50:56.280
Yes, he's playing that word guessing game, Hangman.
没错，他在玩那个猜词游戏，也就是“绞刑架”。

1134
00:50:56.560 --> 00:50:56.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1135
00:50:57.220 --> 00:50:58.240
Kevin's not getting it.
凯文没猜出来。

1136
00:50:58.240 --> 00:50:59.320
No, Kevin's not getting it.
对，凯文没猜出来。

1137
00:50:59.880 --> 00:51:04.760
Lady, this reminded me of Wheel of Fortune.
女士，这让我想起了《幸运轮》。

1138
00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:09.420
Because Wheel of Fortune is based on this game, this, you guess a phrase.
因为《幸运轮》就是基于这个游戏，这个，你来猜一个短语。

1139
00:51:09.980 --> 00:51:13.540
My family was obsessed with Wheel of Fortune.
我家人对《幸运轮》痴迷不已。

1140
00:51:14.300 --> 00:51:18.440
We had the home game, the Wheel of Fortune home game.
我们有家庭版游戏，也就是《幸运轮》家庭游戏。

1141
00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:23.580
And my mom, bless her heart, was a horrible guesser.
我妈妈，好人一个，偏偏是个猜谜白痴。

1142
00:51:23.860 --> 00:51:24.780
Just horrible.
简直糟透了。

1143
00:51:25.240 --> 00:51:29.020
Our favorite family example, you know when you have those things that happen in your family
我们家最经典的例子，你知道那种在家里发生的事，

1144
00:51:29.020 --> 00:51:30.760
that go down as, like, your family lore?
后来成了你们的家族传奇吗？

1145
00:51:30.940 --> 00:51:31.480
Sure, sure.
当然，当然。

1146
00:51:31.660 --> 00:51:31.900
Okay.
好吧。

1147
00:51:32.260 --> 00:51:34.300
We were playing this game.
我们在玩这个游戏。

1148
00:51:34.480 --> 00:51:36.300
My mom's trying to guess the phrase.
我妈妈正试图猜出这个短语。

1149
00:51:37.240 --> 00:51:40.420
And she screams out of nowhere, I've got it!
然后她冷不丁地大喊一声，我知道了！

1150
00:51:40.620 --> 00:51:41.380
I've got it!
我知道了！

1151
00:51:41.540 --> 00:51:42.380
Gold-toothed tiger!
金牙虎！

1152
00:51:42.500 --> 00:51:43.520
Gold-toothed tiger!
金牙虎！

1153
00:51:44.240 --> 00:51:47.500
We're like, Mom, gold-toothed tiger?
我们就说，妈，金牙虎？

1154
00:51:47.640 --> 00:51:51.440
What is this famous phrase, gold-toothed tiger?
这句著名的短语金牙虎是什么意思？

1155
00:51:52.000 --> 00:51:53.660
I don't remember what it was.
我不记得原来是什么了。

1156
00:51:53.820 --> 00:51:55.440
It was not gold-toothed tiger.
根本不是金牙虎。

1157
00:51:55.700 --> 00:51:56.280
No, of course not.
不，当然不是。

1158
00:51:57.080 --> 00:51:59.220
So, anyway, now that's like my sister—
所以，不管怎样，现在这就像我妹妹——

1159
00:51:59.220 --> 00:51:59.720
A catchphrase.
一句口头禅。

1160
00:51:59.720 --> 00:52:02.160
Yeah, my sister and I can be like, gold-toothed tiger, Mom.
对，我和我妹妹可以说，金牙虎，妈。

1161
00:52:02.680 --> 00:52:09.180
But my sister and I became obsessed, and we researched the most common letters in the
但我和我妹妹着迷了，我们研究了英语中最常见的

1162
00:52:09.180 --> 00:52:10.120
English language.
英文字母。

1163
00:52:10.420 --> 00:52:14.560
Wait, isn't one that you're always supposed to guess, like, S or T?
等等，大家不是一直都应该猜那种字母吗，比如 S 或 T？

1164
00:52:15.080 --> 00:52:16.060
T is one.
T 就是其中之一。

1165
00:52:16.200 --> 00:52:16.680
Okay, T.
好的，T。

1166
00:52:16.900 --> 00:52:17.520
I'll tell you.
我来告诉你。

1167
00:52:17.620 --> 00:52:23.880
Here are the 12 most commonly occurring letters in the English language, from most to leaSt.
以下是英语中出现频率最高的 12 个字母，从最多到最少。

1168
00:52:25.640 --> 00:52:37.620
E-T-A-O-I-N-S-H-R-D-L-U.
E-T-A-O-I-N-S-H-R-D-L-U。

1169
00:52:38.300 --> 00:52:42.380
So, if you're ever on Wheel of Fortune, and you're going to buy a vowel, buy an E.
所以，如果你上《幸运轮》，打算买个元音，就买 E。

1170
00:52:42.600 --> 00:52:43.000
Okay.
好的。

1171
00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:46.340
If you're going to guess a consonant, the first one you should guess is T.
如果你要猜辅音，你应该猜的第一个是 T。

1172
00:52:46.520 --> 00:52:46.600
T.
T。

1173
00:52:46.860 --> 00:52:48.040
And the second one is N.
第二个是 N。

1174
00:52:48.040 --> 00:52:52.780
I didn't know that, but I feel like some of it just mushed into my brain because my
我以前不知道，但我觉得其中有些东西已经印在我的脑海里了，因为我

1175
00:52:52.780 --> 00:52:57.000
grandmother faithfully watched Wheel of Fortune every single day.
祖母每天风雨无阻地收看《幸运轮》。

1176
00:52:57.400 --> 00:52:59.280
It was one of her favorite shows.
那是她最喜欢的节目之一。

1177
00:52:59.820 --> 00:53:01.240
She was so good.
她太厉害了。

1178
00:53:01.580 --> 00:53:03.580
She could guess way before everyone else.
她能比其他人早得多地猜出来。

1179
00:53:03.660 --> 00:53:06.040
We used to joke, grandmother, you've got to go on Wheel of Fortune.
我们经常开玩笑，外婆，你得去上《幸运轮》。

1180
00:53:06.140 --> 00:53:08.120
She's like, oh, no, I am not going to be on television.
她说，哦，不，我可不上电视。

1181
00:53:08.840 --> 00:53:09.240
No.
不。

1182
00:53:10.760 --> 00:53:13.640
And she loved Pat Sajak and Vanna White.
她很喜欢帕特·萨贾克和范娜·怀特。

1183
00:53:13.780 --> 00:53:14.760
They could do no wrong.
他们做什么都是对的。

1184
00:53:14.940 --> 00:53:15.160
Oh.
哦。

1185
00:53:15.160 --> 00:53:16.780
And she knew everything about them.
她对他们的事了如指掌。

1186
00:53:17.020 --> 00:53:17.480
Yes.
是的。

1187
00:53:17.680 --> 00:53:18.060
Same.
我也是。

1188
00:53:18.220 --> 00:53:19.280
My family was obsessed.
我的家人都着迷了。

1189
00:53:19.600 --> 00:53:20.500
I love it.
太棒了。

1190
00:53:20.720 --> 00:53:25.880
Just to close this out, I can also tell you the most difficult words to guess.
最后，我还可以告诉你最难猜的单词。

1191
00:53:26.280 --> 00:53:27.060
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

1192
00:53:27.280 --> 00:53:27.460
Yeah.
对。

1193
00:53:27.660 --> 00:53:34.420
This was according to a 2010 study conducted by John McLoon for Wolfram Research.
这是根据沃尔弗拉姆研究公司的约翰·麦克卢恩于 2010 年进行的一项研究。

1194
00:53:34.820 --> 00:53:35.160
Ooh.
哦。

1195
00:53:35.460 --> 00:53:40.040
Why Wolfram Research decided to conduct this survey, I don't know.
沃尔弗拉姆研究公司为什么决定做这项调查，我不知道。

1196
00:53:40.160 --> 00:53:41.820
I don't know, but I appreciate it.
我不知道，但我很感激。

1197
00:53:41.820 --> 00:53:52.800
But the five most difficult words to guess in a word guessing game are jazz, buzz, two Zs,
但在猜字游戏中，最难猜的五个单词是 jazz、buzz，两个 Z，

1198
00:53:53.020 --> 00:53:56.220
haj, fizz, and fuzz.
haj、fizz 和 fuzz。

1199
00:53:56.480 --> 00:53:58.560
People are not good at guessing Z words.
人们不擅长猜带 Z 的单词。

1200
00:53:58.800 --> 00:53:59.420
I guess not.
也是啊。

1201
00:53:59.820 --> 00:54:00.240
Yeah.
对。

1202
00:54:00.540 --> 00:54:03.440
I guess you can use that information if you want.
如果你想用这个信息，我想你随时可以拿去。

1203
00:54:03.560 --> 00:54:03.700
Yeah.
对。

1204
00:54:03.700 --> 00:54:09.020
If it will not help you to guess E-T-A-N-S-H-R-D-L-U.
如果它帮不了你猜出 E-T-A-N-S-H-R-D-L-U 的话。

1205
00:54:09.020 --> 00:54:14.740
I mean, if the caption is like, hot fuzz, zhuzhing jazz, you're like.
我的意思是，如果字幕类似于“热血警探”、“给爵士乐加点料”，你就会觉得……

1206
00:54:17.000 --> 00:54:18.960
Well, no one's going to be able to guess that.
好吧，没人能猜得出来。

1207
00:54:19.300 --> 00:54:19.620
Nope.
没错。

1208
00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:20.620
Make that your phrase.
把这句作为你的口令吧。

1209
00:54:20.780 --> 00:54:22.500
That's your gold tooth tiger right there.
那绝对是你的金牙老虎。

1210
00:54:22.640 --> 00:54:23.400
That's your stumper.
那可真是个难题。

1211
00:54:24.600 --> 00:54:29.980
Michael is going to try to intercept Stanley as he's on his way to meet with a client.
迈克尔打算在斯坦利去见客户的路上拦截他。

1212
00:54:30.460 --> 00:54:35.700
He asked him if he knows a beautiful woman who can dance for a movie Michael is casting.
他问斯坦利认不认识一个会跳舞的美女，来演一部迈克尔正在选角的电影。

1213
00:54:35.700 --> 00:54:39.380
It's going to pay $5 million, some nudity required.
片酬高达五百万美元，有裸露镜头。

1214
00:54:39.660 --> 00:54:48.110
He leaves, and then Jim comes to the window, and he's like, Michael, you need to stop.
他走了之后，吉姆走到窗前，一脸正色地说，迈克尔，你得停下。

1215
00:54:48.590 --> 00:54:49.870
You have to stop this.
你必须停止这种行为。

1216
00:54:49.970 --> 00:54:52.450
You have no proof that Stanley is having an affair.
你没有任何证据证明斯坦利有外遇。

1217
00:54:52.710 --> 00:54:54.630
You might be ruining Stanley's life.
你可能正在毁了斯坦利的生活。

1218
00:54:54.830 --> 00:54:55.030
Yeah.
对。

1219
00:54:55.390 --> 00:54:58.050
We had a fan question, Angela, from Alice R.
安吉拉，我们有一个来自意大利的粉丝爱丽丝·R 的提问，

1220
00:54:58.130 --> 00:54:59.430
in Italy, who said,
她写道：

1221
00:54:59.430 --> 00:55:04.030
at around 7 minutes, 10 seconds, when Michael is talking to Stanley and then Jim through the side
在大约 7 分 10 秒的时候，当迈克尔在办公室侧窗跟斯坦利还有吉姆说话时，

1222
00:55:04.030 --> 00:55:07.630
window of his office, Aaron is sitting in the background.
阿伦一直坐在背景里。

1223
00:55:07.870 --> 00:55:08.630
The whole time.
从头到尾都在。

1224
00:55:08.850 --> 00:55:10.090
And then Allie W.
然后来自加拿大的艾莉·W 说，

1225
00:55:10.330 --> 00:55:11.430
from Canada said,
来自加拿大的人说，

1226
00:55:11.590 --> 00:55:14.470
is there a deleted scene that explains why Aaron is there?
有没有哪个删减片段能解释为什么阿伦会出现在那儿？

1227
00:55:14.790 --> 00:55:20.670
There isn't one on the DVDs, but I can tell you in the shooting draft at the end of this scene,
DVD 里没有，但我可以告诉你，在这个场景结尾的拍摄剧本里，

1228
00:55:21.390 --> 00:55:22.530
Aaron had one line.
阿伦有一句台词。

1229
00:55:22.750 --> 00:55:23.830
What was it?
是什么？

1230
00:55:23.830 --> 00:55:28.590
As Michael considers and runs out, passing by Aaron, Aaron says,
当迈克尔思考完冲出去、从阿伦身边经过时，阿伦说：

1231
00:55:28.790 --> 00:55:30.270
is that the end of the letter?
信到这里就结束了吗？

1232
00:55:30.890 --> 00:55:32.690
Oh, so she was in there.
哦，原来她一直在那儿啊。

1233
00:55:33.590 --> 00:55:37.250
Possibly he was dictating a letter to her to write to someone.
可能当时他在口授一封信，让她写给某个人吧。

1234
00:55:37.590 --> 00:55:39.090
Ah, so good.
啊，太棒了。

1235
00:55:39.550 --> 00:55:43.450
Lady, I think we should take a break, because the scene coming up when Michael runs out and
女士们，我觉得我们该休息一下了，因为接下来迈克尔冲出去上斯坦利车的那个场景，

1236
00:55:43.450 --> 00:55:45.750
gets in Stanley's car, I have a lot to say.
我有太多话想说了。

1237
00:55:45.850 --> 00:55:46.630
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1238
00:55:46.770 --> 00:55:47.610
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1239
00:55:47.630 --> 00:55:48.570
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

1240
00:55:56.900 --> 00:55:58.980
Hi, I'm Jessica St. Clair.
嗨，我是杰西卡·圣克莱尔。

1241
00:55:58.980 --> 00:56:03.780
And I'm June Diane Raphael, and we are two friends trying to survive the chaos
我是琼·黛安·拉斐尔，我们是两个努力在生活带来的混乱中求生存、

1242
00:56:03.780 --> 00:56:06.940
and celebrate the joy that life throws our way.
同时庆祝生活给予我们的快乐的朋友。

1243
00:56:07.040 --> 00:56:10.200
And we do it every week on our podcast, The Deep Dive.
我们每周都会在我们的播客《深度潜水》中这么做。

1244
00:56:10.440 --> 00:56:14.660
Sometimes we dig into the deep stuff, like how I communicate with my dead best friend.
有时我们会探讨深刻的话题，比如我和我去世的挚友是怎么沟通的。

1245
00:56:14.860 --> 00:56:18.700
And sometimes we give bad advice based off a TikTok I saw,
有时我们会根据我在 TikTok 上看到的内容给出糟糕的建议，

1246
00:56:18.820 --> 00:56:20.780
and we're not going to apologize for that.
而我们对此绝不道歉。

1247
00:56:20.940 --> 00:56:21.860
Absolutely not.
绝对不。

1248
00:56:22.060 --> 00:56:25.440
You'll laugh, you'll cry, you'll hire a psychic medium.
你会大笑，你会痛哭，你还会去请个通灵师。

1249
00:56:25.780 --> 00:56:26.820
Join us, won't you?
加入我们吧，好吗？

1250
00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:30.520
Listen to The Deep Dive wherever you get your podcasts, from Lemonada Media.
在 Lemonada Media 收听《深度潜水》，随时随地获取你的播客。

1251
00:56:38.920 --> 00:56:41.000
Michael runs into the parking lot.
迈克尔跑进了停车场。

1252
00:56:41.160 --> 00:56:45.560
He stops Stanley from driving away by throwing himself in front of Stanley's car,
他扑到斯坦利的汽车前面，阻止斯坦利开车离开，

1253
00:56:45.580 --> 00:56:47.780
and then he says, are you having an affair?
然后他说，你是不是有外遇了？

1254
00:56:48.160 --> 00:56:50.660
Cut to, now he's in the car.
镜头一转，现在他坐在车里。

1255
00:56:50.900 --> 00:56:51.340
Right.
没错。

1256
00:56:52.620 --> 00:56:58.740
And believe it or not, Stanley admits he's having an affair with Cynthia, his nurse.
信不信由你，斯坦利承认他和自己的护士辛西娅有染。

1257
00:56:59.080 --> 00:57:01.400
They had long walks on the treadmill together.
他们一起在跑步机上长时间地散步。

1258
00:57:01.920 --> 00:57:04.220
You know, Terry's been traveling so much.
你知道的，泰瑞出差太多了。

1259
00:57:04.220 --> 00:57:05.280
He's been lonely.
他一直很孤独。

1260
00:57:05.760 --> 00:57:07.040
Michael is still not getting it.
迈克尔还是没明白。

1261
00:57:07.300 --> 00:57:12.620
But then Stanley is like, I'm actually on my way to break it off with Cynthia right now.
但接着斯坦利说，其实我正准备现在就去和辛西娅分手。

1262
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:16.120
And Michael's like, wait a second, you said you were going on a sales call.
迈克尔就说，等一下，你刚才说你是去拜访客户。

1263
00:57:16.220 --> 00:57:17.380
Do people do that all the time?
大家平时都这样吗？

1264
00:57:17.520 --> 00:57:20.240
Do they tell me they're going on sales calls and they go somewhere else?
他们会告诉我他们是去拜访客户，然后去别的地方吗？

1265
00:57:20.580 --> 00:57:21.440
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

1266
00:57:21.440 --> 00:57:24.400
And then Michael is like, wow, it's true.
然后迈克尔就想，哇，这是真的。

1267
00:57:25.020 --> 00:57:26.640
He finally gets it.
他终于明白了。

1268
00:57:26.820 --> 00:57:31.240
And Stanley's like, listen, you cannot tell anyone about this, please.
斯坦利就说，听着，你千万不能把这件事告诉任何人，拜托了。

1269
00:57:31.500 --> 00:57:32.760
I'm counting on you.
我指望你了。

1270
00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:37.560
So in the shooting of this scene, Angela, I counted four cameras.
所以在拍摄这场戏的时候，安吉拉，我数了数有四个镜头。

1271
00:57:37.860 --> 00:57:43.060
We usually only have two cameras, but I counted four different camera angles.
我们平时通常只有两个镜头，但我数了四个不同的机位。

1272
00:57:43.240 --> 00:57:44.520
Give it to me, lady.
快告诉我，女士。

1273
00:57:44.620 --> 00:57:45.300
Where'd you see them?
你在哪看到的？

1274
00:57:45.300 --> 00:57:46.280
To cover this scene.
为了拍摄这场戏。

1275
00:57:46.480 --> 00:57:53.360
So the first one is shooting from up above, out of the office, down onto the parking lot.
所以第一个是从上面拍摄，从办公室外面朝下拍停车场。

1276
00:57:54.280 --> 00:58:01.540
Then we have the bulk of the scene, which is shooting either through the window on Stanley's side
然后我们有这场戏的大部分内容，要么是从斯坦利这一侧的车窗拍进去，

1277
00:58:01.540 --> 00:58:05.700
or the other side shooting through the window on Michael's side.
要么是从另一侧从迈克尔这一侧的车窗拍进去。

1278
00:58:05.700 --> 00:58:06.500
So that's three.
所以那是三个。

1279
00:58:06.500 --> 00:58:15.080
But then for one second, right around eight minutes, 27 seconds, there is this spy shot that is straight on.
但在大约八分二十七秒的时候，有一秒钟，有这样一个正面的偷拍镜头。

1280
00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:18.400
And it's sort of through some leaves.
而且有点像是透过一些树叶拍的。

1281
00:58:19.080 --> 00:58:19.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1282
00:58:20.020 --> 00:58:23.800
Well, Randy told me that this was a trick.
好吧，兰迪告诉我这其实是个把戏。

1283
00:58:24.040 --> 00:58:24.800
There's nothing there.
根本没有那棵树。

1284
00:58:25.060 --> 00:58:25.640
Fakie tree?
假树？

1285
00:58:25.880 --> 00:58:26.640
Fakie tree.
假树。

1286
00:58:27.000 --> 00:58:27.620
Yes.
是的。

1287
00:58:28.640 --> 00:58:38.160
They took a leafy branch and they put it on a grip stand and then someone would shake it a little bit to make it seem like there was a breeze.
他们拿了一根带叶子的树枝放在灯光支架上，然后有人会轻轻摇晃它，让人觉得有微风吹过。

1288
00:58:38.880 --> 00:58:44.720
And Matt composed his shot to include some of those leaves so that it would look like a spy shot.
马特构图时把其中的一些树叶拍了进去，这样看起来就像是个偷拍镜头。

1289
00:58:44.900 --> 00:58:50.000
Why in my brain do I hear someone like on a walkie-talkie going, shake it a little less.
为什么我脑海里会听到有人拿着对讲机说，少摇一点。

1290
00:58:50.500 --> 00:58:51.640
Yeah, it's too much movement.
对，动静太大了。

1291
00:58:51.840 --> 00:58:52.480
Too much shaking.
晃动得太厉害了。

1292
00:58:53.180 --> 00:58:54.360
Shake it up higher.
往高处晃。

1293
00:58:54.960 --> 00:58:55.960
Shake it lower.
往低处晃。

1294
00:58:57.060 --> 00:59:02.960
Now, I don't know if Randy was teasing me, but he told me the technical term for this is called a branch-a-loris.
现在，我不知道兰迪是不是在捉弄我，但他告诉我这个术语叫“树枝假障眼法”。

1295
00:59:03.200 --> 00:59:03.940
Come on.
别开玩笑了。

1296
00:59:04.160 --> 00:59:06.660
He said it's often used in outdoor shooting.
他说这经常用在户外拍摄中。

1297
00:59:06.900 --> 00:59:07.440
Come on.
拜托。

1298
00:59:07.460 --> 00:59:08.100
Is that true?
那是真的吗？

1299
00:59:08.220 --> 00:59:08.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

1300
00:59:08.980 --> 00:59:10.560
Randy, a branch-a-loris.
兰迪，还“树枝假障眼法”。

1301
00:59:10.780 --> 00:59:12.420
Is he listening to our podcast?
他在听我们的播客吗？

1302
00:59:12.500 --> 00:59:13.120
Just laughing.
只是在笑。

1303
00:59:13.120 --> 00:59:14.020
He's like, they bought it.
他就像是在说，他们居然买账了。

1304
00:59:14.620 --> 00:59:15.860
Branch-a-loris.
树懒罗莉丝。

1305
00:59:16.260 --> 00:59:17.440
That's so fun.
太有趣了。

1306
00:59:17.600 --> 00:59:23.600
If I'm ever directing Randy and I call for a branch-a-a-loris and people don't know what I'm talking about, I'm calling you.
如果以后我导演兰迪的戏时，喊出了“树懒罗莉丝”而大家不知道我在说什么，我就打电话找你。

1307
00:59:24.640 --> 00:59:29.700
Well, Michael is going to promise Stanley that he won't say anything, but we already know it's too late for that.
迈克尔答应了斯坦利绝不说出去，但我们都知道现在为时已晚。

1308
00:59:29.920 --> 00:59:38.780
So now he comes up with this crazy idea that what he has to do is diffuse that one piece of information by just throwing out all kinds of rumors.
所以他想出了一个疯狂的主意，觉得必须通过散布各种各样的谣言来冲淡那条真实信息。

1309
00:59:39.220 --> 00:59:39.440
Yeah.
对。

1310
00:59:39.720 --> 00:59:43.200
He finds Kevin in the kitchen making cookies?
他发现凯文在厨房里烤饼干？

1311
00:59:43.680 --> 00:59:46.360
Yeah, he's making cookies in the toaster oven.
对，他在小烤箱里烤饼干。

1312
00:59:47.260 --> 00:59:53.080
Michael says, have you heard about Angela dating an 81-year-old billionaire who owns a Quiznos?
迈克尔说，你听说安吉拉在和一个拥有一家奎兹诺斯三明治店的81岁亿万富翁约会吗？

1313
00:59:53.500 --> 00:59:58.200
Then he goes up to reception and he tells Aaron that Kelly is an anorexia tick.
然后他走到前台，告诉亚伦凯莉得了厌食症。

1314
00:59:58.580 --> 01:00:06.880
Did you notice at 10 minutes, 25 seconds that Aaron's little desk area has a Keystone College little banner?
你有没有注意到在10分25秒时，亚伦的小前台区域挂着一个小小的基斯通学院横幅？

1315
01:00:07.140 --> 01:00:07.520
Yes.
注意到了。

1316
01:00:07.740 --> 01:00:09.880
And a teddy bear with a red hoodie.
还有一个穿着红色连帽衫的小熊。

1317
01:00:10.080 --> 01:00:12.780
I got real interested in her reception desk, Angela.
安吉拉，我对她的前台桌子真的产生了浓厚兴趣。

1318
01:00:12.880 --> 01:00:13.900
Oh, did you?
哦，是吗？

1319
01:00:13.900 --> 01:00:20.560
You and I obviously were thinking the same thing because when I saw that Keystone College banner, I was like, hold up.
显然你和我想的一样，因为当我看到那个基斯通学院横幅时，我就想，等等。

1320
01:00:20.820 --> 01:00:23.400
I want to know more about Aaron.
我想多了解一下亚伦。

1321
01:00:23.640 --> 01:00:24.920
What will her desk reveal?
她的办公桌会透露出什么？

1322
01:00:25.140 --> 01:00:26.160
What did you find?
你发现了什么？

1323
01:00:26.560 --> 01:00:31.020
Well, Keystone College is a real private college in northwestern Pennsylvania.
基斯通学院是宾夕法尼亚州西北部的一所真正的私立大学。

1324
01:00:31.880 --> 01:00:37.000
And not only does she have a stuffed dog with a little sweater, that little sweater says J-Rob.
不仅她有一个穿着小毛衣的毛绒狗，那件小毛衣上还写着J-Rob。

1325
01:00:37.000 --> 01:00:43.500
And then she has a pink ski boot, mug, that she has put her pens and pencils in.
然后她还有一个粉色滑雪靴造型的马克杯，她把钢笔和铅笔放在里面。

1326
01:00:43.620 --> 01:00:46.060
And that also says J-Rob.
上面也写着J-Rob。

1327
01:00:46.440 --> 01:00:47.780
What is J-Rob?
J-Rob是什么？

1328
01:00:48.420 --> 01:00:49.620
I googled it.
我谷歌了一下。

1329
01:00:49.780 --> 01:00:52.520
And it is a wrestling camp in Pennsylvania.
它是宾夕法尼亚州的一个摔跤营。

1330
01:00:52.860 --> 01:00:53.440
Get out.
少来这一套。

1331
01:00:53.820 --> 01:00:55.680
I don't think this is correct.
我觉得这不对劲。

1332
01:00:56.020 --> 01:00:58.020
Why they would sell a ski boot.
他们为什么会卖滑雪靴呢。

1333
01:00:58.080 --> 01:01:00.880
I looked at all their merch for this wrestling camp.
我查看了这个摔跤营所有的周边商品。

1334
01:01:01.080 --> 01:01:03.100
I don't even think the logo is the same.
我甚至觉得标志都不一样。

1335
01:01:03.340 --> 01:01:05.060
Did Aaron go to wrestling camp?
亚伦去过摔跤营吗？

1336
01:01:05.060 --> 01:01:06.800
I am very stumped on this one.
这个问题真把我难住了。

1337
01:01:06.960 --> 01:01:07.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

1338
01:01:07.980 --> 01:01:12.300
But Aaron also has a candy dish with some individually wrapped lifesavers in it.
但亚伦还有一个糖果盘，里面装了一些独立包装的救生圈牌糖果。

1339
01:01:12.640 --> 01:01:13.960
Phil Shea, what is J-Rob?
菲尔·谢伊，J-Rob是什么？

1340
01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:15.480
What is J-Rob?
J-Rob是什么？

1341
01:01:15.500 --> 01:01:18.060
And then I was like, is it J-R-B-B?
然后我想，是J-R-B-B吗？

1342
01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:19.980
Like J-R-B-B?
就像J-R-B-B那样？

1343
01:01:20.220 --> 01:01:21.960
Or is it J-R-O-B?
还是J-R-O-B？

1344
01:01:22.680 --> 01:01:24.100
I googled both.
我两个都搜了。

1345
01:01:24.300 --> 01:01:27.720
But there is a wrestling camp in Pennsylvania called J-Rob.
但宾夕法尼亚州确实有一个叫J-Rob的摔跤营。

1346
01:01:27.720 --> 01:01:28.300
Okay.
好吧。

1347
01:01:29.300 --> 01:01:31.360
Michael's going to continue his rumor mill.
迈克尔要继续他的造谣大业了。

1348
01:01:31.620 --> 01:01:38.120
He's going to tell Kelly that Aaron isn't a very good worker and may not last long at Dundra Mifflin and that Andy is gay.
他要告诉凯莉，亚伦工作表现不太好，可能在邓德米夫林干不长，还说安迪是同性恋。

1349
01:01:38.320 --> 01:01:40.300
He tells Meredith that Pam is pregnant.
他告诉梅雷迪思说帕姆怀孕了。

1350
01:01:40.820 --> 01:01:43.280
So he's really throwing a lot of stuff out there.
所以他真的是在到处散布各种消息。

1351
01:01:43.420 --> 01:01:46.600
Of course, we know, oh my gosh, Pam is pregnant.
当然，我们都知道，天哪，帕姆怀孕了。

1352
01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:47.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1353
01:01:47.760 --> 01:01:51.500
Well, now the rumors are just traveling all crazy throughout the office.
嗯，现在办公室里的谣言传得乱七八糟的。

1354
01:01:51.500 --> 01:01:51.980
Yes.
没错。

1355
01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:55.440
And now people are going to start hearing the rumors about themselves.
而且现在大家开始听到关于他们自己的谣言了。

1356
01:01:55.840 --> 01:01:56.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1357
01:01:56.260 --> 01:01:58.800
Andy hears this rumor that he might be gay.
安迪听到一个传闻，说他可能是个同性恋。

1358
01:01:59.000 --> 01:01:59.680
From Kevin.
从凯文那听来的。

1359
01:01:59.720 --> 01:02:01.000
And he's like, was this Broccoli Rob?
然后他就想，这是西兰花罗布说的吗？

1360
01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:01.740
Yes.
没错。

1361
01:02:01.940 --> 01:02:02.900
Was it someone in high school?
是高中时的某个人吗？

1362
01:02:03.120 --> 01:02:05.940
This sends Andy on an existential crisis.
这让安迪陷入了一场存在主义危机。

1363
01:02:06.640 --> 01:02:09.500
And he's going to confront Oscar in the break room.
他打算去休息室找奥斯卡对质。

1364
01:02:09.700 --> 01:02:11.540
Oscar has such a great talking head.
奥斯卡的那段单人访谈太精彩了。

1365
01:02:11.780 --> 01:02:17.760
After that scene with Andy where he's like, what, it's my responsibility to comfort the insecure heterosexual men?
在拍完那场安迪质问他的戏后，他说，什么，安慰那些没有安全感的异性恋男人是我的责任吗？

1366
01:02:17.960 --> 01:02:19.480
That can't possibly fall on me.
这总不能落到我头上吧。

1367
01:02:19.480 --> 01:02:22.160
I'm paraphrasing it, but it's something like that.
我这是意译，但差不多就是这意思。

1368
01:02:22.240 --> 01:02:22.900
It's so good.
太棒了。

1369
01:02:23.160 --> 01:02:29.380
When Andy is describing this scenario where Brad Pitt is like coming on to him.
当安迪描述布拉德·皮特向他示好的那个场景时。

1370
01:02:29.460 --> 01:02:30.680
At like a beach cabana.
就在海滩小屋那边。

1371
01:02:31.080 --> 01:02:36.060
And Brad Pitt is trying to kiss him and Andy resists, but Brad Pitt keeps coming for him.
布拉德·皮特试图吻他，安迪反抗了，但布拉德·皮特步步紧逼。

1372
01:02:36.660 --> 01:02:44.840
Oscar has this amazing line where he says, so if you resisted Brad Pitt a little bit, he would still need to get to you.
奥斯卡有一句绝妙的台词，他说，所以如果你稍微反抗一下布拉德·皮特，他还是会想方设法得到你。

1373
01:02:46.920 --> 01:02:56.440
So, lady, the mention of Brad Pitt made me very randomly think about how I have had recurring dreams about Brad Pitt making me soup.
所以，女士们，提到布拉德·皮特让我莫名其妙地想起我曾多次梦见布拉德·皮特给我做汤。

1374
01:02:56.660 --> 01:02:57.060
What?
什么？

1375
01:02:57.280 --> 01:02:58.700
He makes me soup.
他给我做汤。

1376
01:02:58.840 --> 01:03:00.000
What does this mean?
这代表什么意思？

1377
01:03:01.600 --> 01:03:02.560
Recurring dream.
反复出现的梦。

1378
01:03:02.720 --> 01:03:03.880
Like over your life?
贯穿你的生活那种？

1379
01:03:04.020 --> 01:03:04.400
Yes.
对。

1380
01:03:04.600 --> 01:03:06.080
Like since college.
从大学开始就这样。

1381
01:03:06.380 --> 01:03:06.900
What?
什么？

1382
01:03:07.460 --> 01:03:11.580
And Brad Pitt would make me a warm, comforting bowl of soup.
而且布拉德·皮特会给我做一碗温暖、治愈的汤。

1383
01:03:11.740 --> 01:03:13.240
And it would make me happy.
那会让我感到快乐。

1384
01:03:13.240 --> 01:03:15.440
And he was my friend in my dreaMs.
在我的梦里，他是我的朋友。

1385
01:03:15.620 --> 01:03:16.580
Was he fully clothed?
他穿好衣服了吗？

1386
01:03:16.740 --> 01:03:17.160
Yes.
穿了。

1387
01:03:17.540 --> 01:03:17.900
Okay.
好吧。

1388
01:03:18.020 --> 01:03:19.920
It was just a wonderful gesture.
这真是一个美妙的举动。

1389
01:03:20.420 --> 01:03:25.560
So, I looked up, you know, dreams and meaning of dreaMs.
所以，我查了一下，你知道的，关于梦和梦的含义。

1390
01:03:25.800 --> 01:03:27.660
What does it mean if you have soup in your dream?
梦里出现汤是什么意思？

1391
01:03:27.660 --> 01:03:33.720
Well, what a celebrity in your dream is, is that the celebrity is you.
嗯，梦里的名人其实就是你自己。

1392
01:03:34.020 --> 01:03:36.460
It's like a version of you.
就像是另一个版本的你。

1393
01:03:36.740 --> 01:03:39.780
So, you are Brad Pitt and you're making yourself soup?
所以，你是布拉德·皮特，然后你在给自己做汤？

1394
01:03:39.940 --> 01:03:40.920
I guess so.
我猜是吧。

1395
01:03:40.920 --> 01:03:44.620
But more than that, here's what I determined it to be.
但不仅于此，我是这么确定的。

1396
01:03:44.960 --> 01:03:45.180
Okay.
好吧。

1397
01:03:45.500 --> 01:03:46.900
Brad Pitt is from Missouri.
布拉德·皮特来自密苏里州。

1398
01:03:47.580 --> 01:03:49.240
He's from where I grew up.
他来自我长大的地方。

1399
01:03:49.300 --> 01:03:50.740
So, I think.
所以，我觉得。

1400
01:03:50.880 --> 01:03:53.520
He was the big local celebrity when you were growing up.
在你成长的时候，他是当地的大明星。

1401
01:03:53.520 --> 01:03:58.980
He went to Mizzou, which was the college about an hour and a half away from my college.
他去了密苏里大学，那所大学离我上大学的地方大约有一个半小时的车程。

1402
01:03:59.160 --> 01:04:00.100
He didn't finish.
他没读完。

1403
01:04:00.440 --> 01:04:02.860
But then he went off and he became a big star.
但后来他离开了，成了一个大明星。

1404
01:04:03.320 --> 01:04:04.720
You know, I've never met him.
你知道的，我从未见过他。

1405
01:04:04.820 --> 01:04:08.060
I've never been able to geek out with him about our Missouri roots.
我从来没有机会跟他狂热地聊聊我们共同的密苏里根基。

1406
01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:09.740
But it was a big deal.
但这可是一件大事。

1407
01:04:09.860 --> 01:04:13.080
Like when you're from Missouri and someone else from Missouri is super famous.
就像当你来自密苏里，而另一个来自密苏里的人超级有名时。

1408
01:04:13.340 --> 01:04:14.660
Like everybody knows it, you know?
就像人人都知道，你知道吗？

1409
01:04:15.260 --> 01:04:15.920
Oh, man.
天哪。

1410
01:04:15.960 --> 01:04:17.660
I can never meet him now.
我现在永远不能见他了。

1411
01:04:18.020 --> 01:04:18.440
Why?
为什么？

1412
01:04:18.820 --> 01:04:20.500
Because I know me.
因为我了解我自己。

1413
01:04:20.680 --> 01:04:21.640
You're going to say something.
你会说些什么的。

1414
01:04:21.640 --> 01:04:25.360
And I know if I meet Brad Pitt, yeah, I won't be able to.
我知道如果我见到布拉德·皮特，是的，我会无法克制。

1415
01:04:25.580 --> 01:04:27.060
It'll be like a Michael Scott moment.
那会像是迈克尔·斯科特式的社死瞬间。

1416
01:04:27.060 --> 01:04:30.860
I'll say, my friend Jenna dreams that you make her soup.
我会说，我的朋友珍娜梦想着你给她做汤。

1417
01:04:32.680 --> 01:04:34.440
